//? Title: SipHash-2-4: actual keyed ARX rounds
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A hash table needs a keyed short-input hash to make deliberately chosen bucket
collisions difficult for someone without the key. SipHash-2-4 maps raw bytes and
a128-bit key to64 bits using additions, rotations and XOR. We expose actual
round words, retain the original reference vectors and32-word bucket experiment,
and avoid treating a tiny histogram as a security proof.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

Initialize four64-bit words by XORing key halves with fixed constants. Each full
little-endian message word is XORed into v3, followed by two SipRounds, then
XORed into v0. A compulsory final word contains the remaining bytes and the
message length modulo256 in its top byte. After absorbing it, XOR ff into v2 and
run four final rounds. The result XORs all four words.

$$ B=\lfloor L/8\rfloor+1,\qquad R=2B+4.$$
\alttext(Length L uses floor L divided by eight plus one absorbed blocks and twice that many rounds plus four.)

Additions wrap modulo2^64, rotations preserve all bits, and XOR mixes state
dependencies. Even empty input uses one tail block and six rounds. Time is
linear in message bytes, with constant working storage unless actual round
states are captured. A64-bit output has birthday collisions around2^32 random
evaluations; it is not a collision-resistant content digest. Secret keys
mitigate predictable hash-table flooding but do not make collisions impossible.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/siphash_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::siphash24_trace(a::siphash_example_key(), "");
    std::print("| block | finalization | round | actual words before | actual words after |\n| ---: | --- | " "---: | --- | --- |\n");
    for (const auto &s : r.history)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | `{}` | `{}` |\n", s.block, s.finalization,
                   s.round, s.before, s.after);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Reference key00 through0f; empty bytes");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} blocks, {} actual rounds", r.blocks,
                                     r.rounds));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0}, std::format("Hash {:016x}", r.hash));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/siphash_tiny.svg");
}
```
